# ❤️ Heart Disease – Data Science & Machine Learning Analysis

## 📌 Project Overview

This project focuses on performing comprehensive Data Science analysis on a Heart Disease dataset using Python. It explores healthcare data to identify meaningful patterns, understand relationships between medical attributes, and investigate factors associated with heart disease.

The project covers the complete Data Science workflow, starting from data preprocessing and Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) to statistical analysis, dimensionality reduction, and Machine Learning techniques.

## 🎯 Objectives
- Understand the structure and characteristics of the Heart Disease dataset.
- Perform Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) to identify patterns and relationships.
- Apply statistical techniques to analyze numerical features.
- Perform data preprocessing and feature analysis.
- Implement PCA and SVD for dimensionality reduction.
- Visualize important patterns and correlations.
- Explore data-driven approaches for heart disease analysis.

## 🛠️ Technologies & Libraries
- Python
- NumPy
- Pandas
- Matplotlib
- Seaborn
- Scikit-learn
- Jupyter Notebook / Google Colab

## 📊 Operations & Techniques Performed

### 1. Data Loading & Understanding
- Dataset loading and inspection
- Dataset dimensions and data types
- Statistical summary
- Missing value identification

### 2. Data Preprocessing
- Missing value handling
- Duplicate detection
- Data cleaning
- Feature scaling and standardization

### 3. Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)
- Univariate and multivariate analysis
- Distribution plots and histograms
- Box plots and outlier detection
- Correlation matrix and heatmaps
- Feature-wise comparisons

### 4. Statistical Analysis
- Mean, median, mode, and standard deviation
- Variance and distribution analysis
- Correlation analysis
- Statistical interpretation of medical attributes

### 5. Dimensionality Reduction
- Principal Component Analysis (PCA)
- Singular Value Decomposition (SVD)
- Explained variance analysis
- Principal component visualization
- Dimensionality reduction and feature representation

### 6. Data Visualization
- Histograms
- Scatter plots
- Box plots
- Heatmaps
- PCA and SVD visualizations

### 7. Machine Learning Analysis
- Feature selection and transformation
- Model preparation
- Model evaluation using appropriate performance metrics (where implemented)

## 📈 Key Learning Outcomes
- Practical understanding of the complete Data Science workflow.
- Experience in analyzing healthcare datasets.
- Understanding of statistical relationships in medical data.
- Hands-on implementation of PCA and SVD.
- Improved skills in Python-based data analysis and visualization.
- Understanding how data science techniques can support healthcare research.

## ⚠️ Disclaimer
This project is developed for educational and research purposes only. The analysis is not intended for medical diagnosis or clinical decision-making.

---
**Domain:** Healthcare | Data Science | Machine Learning

**Focus:** Data Analysis • EDA • Statistics • PCA • SVD • Feature Engineering • Visualization
